# Vitest Testing Standard (HW3)

Scoped to NestJS/Angular implementation under `homework-3/platform/`. **Not Hono.**

1. All newly created test files must use **Vitest**.
2. Do not use **Jest**, `node:test`, or `node:assert` in HW3 platform tests.
3. Prefer importing `describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi` from `vitest`.
4. Run tests via each package `npm test` script (Vitest config in workspace).
5. NestJS HTTP integration: use **`@nestjs/testing` + supertest** on `app.getHttpServer()` — not Hono `app.request()`.
6. Map tests to [`docs/testing/testing-strategy.md`](../../docs/testing/testing-strategy.md) and Mars Family fixtures in [`mocks/`](../../mocks/).
7. Assert request/response shapes against [`docs/api/openapi/`](../../docs/api/openapi/) where applicable.
8. See [`homework-3/.cursor/skills/vitest-testing/SKILL.md`](../skills/vitest-testing/SKILL.md) and [`docs/architecture/monorepo-and-tooling.md`](../../docs/architecture/monorepo-and-tooling.md).
